<h2>The Complete Guide to Hiring a 9 Seater Tempo Traveller in Bangalore</h2>
<p>A group of eight or nine people is too big for any car and too small for a large van, and that is exactly where the 9 seater Tempo Traveller fits. This guide covers what the vehicle offers, who books it, how seats and luggage work, what real trips cost, how it compares with an Innova Crysta and with hiring two cars, and how to plan the day. All rates are the live Yogi Tours &amp; Travels tariff: ₹28 per km with AC, a 300 km daily minimum and ₹500 per day driver Bata, with tolls, parking, permits and state taxes billed at actuals.</p>

<h2>Part 1. The Vehicle</h2>
<p>The 9 seater Tempo Traveller is a Force Traveller with forward-facing push-back seats in a 1x1 and 2x1 layout, individual windows, reading lights, charging points, an audio system and a dedicated luggage boot with a roof carrier. It carries nine passengers plus the driver and about nine bags. It is air-conditioned, with individual louvers, and it is the smallest vehicle in the Tempo Traveller range.</p>
<p>The advantage of the 9 seater over the larger Travellers is manoeuvrability and cost. It is easier to park, easier on narrow roads and cheaper per km than the 12 and 17 seaters, while still seating a group that no car can carry. The trade-off is that it uses the traditional Traveller body, so the ride is that of a sturdy van and not the car-like feel of an <a href="/force-urbania">Urbania</a>.</p>

<h3>What is inside</h3>
<ul>
<li>Forward-facing push-back seats that tilt for rest.</li>
<li>Individual windows with tinted glass.</li>
<li>Individual AC louvers.</li>
<li>Reading lights and charging points.</li>
<li>An audio system.</li>
<li>A luggage boot plus a roof carrier.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Part 2. Who Books a 9 Seater</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Two families travelling together,</strong> where eight or nine people with luggage will not fit in two cars comfortably.</li>
<li><strong>Office teams and client groups</strong> of up to nine, on outings and site visits. See <a href="/services/corporate-travel">corporate travel</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Friend groups</strong> on weekend getaways to Coorg, Chikmagalur and Wayanad.</li>
<li><strong>Pilgrimage groups</strong> to Tirupati, Dharmasthala, Murudeshwar and Kukke. See <a href="/services/pilgrimage-tours">pilgrimage tours</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Airport groups</strong> arriving with too much luggage for one car. See <a href="/services/airport-transfer">airport transfer</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Wedding guests,</strong> moving relatives between the venue, hotels and homes. See <a href="/services/wedding-transportation">wedding transportation</a>.</li>
</ul>

