<h2>Part 6. Planning Tips</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Fix the headcount.</strong> Nine is the limit. For ten or more, choose the <a href="/fleet/tempo-traveller/maharaja-tempo-traveller">12 seater</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Count bags.</strong> About nine bags fit in the boot and roof carrier. Keep valuables in the cabin.</li>
<li><strong>Choose one coordinator.</strong> One person handles the list, the receipts and the driver.</li>
<li><strong>Plan the pickups.</strong> Area pages include <a href="/9seater-tempotraveller/whitefield">Whitefield</a>, <a href="/9seater-tempotraveller/koramangala">Koramangala</a>, <a href="/9seater-tempotraveller/indiranagar">Indiranagar</a> and <a href="/9seater-tempotraveller/hsr-layout">HSR Layout</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Start early.</strong> A 5:00 or 6:00 AM start avoids the worst traffic.</li>
<li><strong>Leave room for stops.</strong> Allow half an hour for breakfast and an hour for lunch.</li>
<li><strong>Get the quotation in writing,</strong> with rate, daily minimum, Bata and extras.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Part 7. Comfort, Safety and Seasons</h2>
<ul>
<li>Seat elderly passengers and those prone to motion sickness in front.</li>
<li>Take a break every two hours, and listen if the driver advises against a late-night dash.</li>
<li>Keep medicines, documents and chargers in the cabin.</li>
<li>November to February is the best season and the busiest. March to May suits hill stations. June to September is green but wet, and slower on the roads.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Part 8. Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
<ol>
<li>Booking a 9 seater for ten people.</li>
<li>Booking a Tempo Traveller for seven when an Innova Crysta would cost less.</li>
<li>Not counting bags.</li>
<li>Comparing only the per-km rate.</li>
<li>Returning after 10:00 PM and paying extra Bata.</li>
<li>Skipping the written quotation.</li>
<li>Forgetting interstate permits.</li>
<li>Booking late for peak dates.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Part 9. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><strong>How many people does a 9 seater carry?</strong> Nine passengers plus the driver.</p>
<p><strong>What is the rate?</strong> ₹28 per km with AC, a 300 km daily minimum and ₹500 per day Bata.</p>
<p><strong>How much luggage fits?</strong> About nine bags.</p>
<p><strong>Is it cheaper than two cars?</strong> For eight or nine people, usually yes, because it means one driver and one set of tolls.</p>
<p><strong>Can we go to Coorg, Ooty, Mysore or Tirupati?</strong> Yes. Interstate permits are in the quotation.</p>
<p><strong>Is there a 12 seater?</strong> Yes, the <a href="/fleet/tempo-traveller/maharaja-tempo-traveller">12 seater Maharaja Tempo Traveller</a> at ₹22 per km.</p>
<p><strong>Can I get a GST invoice?</strong> Yes, on request.</p>
<p><strong>How do I book?</strong> Call +91 97410 32020 or WhatsApp +91 98867 70099, or <a href="/contact">send an enquiry</a>.</p>

